{
  "rules": [
    "Correct for severe mean reversion: The model consistently fails to anticipate sharp price drops following volatility spikes (e.g., the drop from ~76 to ~70 in late May), often maintaining a flat or slightly upward trajectory while true prices fall 5-8 EUR below forecast.",
    "Adjust for sentiment lag: Positive sentiment spikes (values of 1.00) are followed by immediate price surges that the model misses; the model reacts too slowly to bullish news, resulting in underestimation in the first 3-5 days of a positive sentiment window.",
    "Reduce long-horizon bias: The model exhibits a persistent upward drift in its 30-day forecast regardless of recent downward trends; apply a downward correction factor of 2-4 EUR for forecasts beyond day 10 when the 18-day history shows a declining or volatile pattern.",
    "Overshoot correction after peaks: When history shows a peak followed by a decline (e.g., 76.67), the model incorrectly predicts a recovery or stability; force a downward adjustment in the forecast for days 15-25 to align with the observed mean-reverting behavior.",
    "Sentiment-weighted volatility: Ignore positive sentiment signals if the immediate 5-day price history shows a downward trend; the model overweights isolated positive sentiment events without accounting for the broader bearish momentum."
  ]
}
